# Day 7: GitHub Pull Request 

## 1. GitHub Collaboration
GitHub collaboration allows multiple developers to work
on a project, share code, review changes, and fix issues.

## 2. Feature Branch
A feature branch is a separate branch used to develop
features or make changes without directly modifying main.

## 3. Pull Request (PR)
A Pull Request is a request to review and merge changes
from one branch into another branch on GitHub.

## 4. Code Review
Code review is the process of checking proposed code
changes for errors, quality, security, and maintainability.

## 5. Pull Request Workflow
1. Create a feature branch.
2. Make code changes.
3. Commit the changes.
4. Push the branch to GitHub.
5. Open a Pull Request.
6. Review and discuss the changes.
7. Approve and merge the Pull Request.

## 6. Git Merge vs Pull Request
Git Merge combines changes from one branch into another.
A Pull Request is a collaboration and review process
provided by platforms such as GitHub.

## 7. Fork
A fork is a personal copy of another user's repository
under your GitHub account.

## 8. Issues
GitHub Issues are used to track bugs, tasks, questions,
and feature requests.

